---
import PrivacyLayout from "../../components/PrivacyLayout.astro";
---

<PrivacyLayout
    title="Privacy Policy - Denaro App"
    appName="Denaro"
    lastUpdated="1 August 2026"
    accentColor="#3498db"
>
    <div class="my-5 rounded-md border-l-4 border-emerald-500/80 bg-emerald-50/70 dark:bg-emerald-500/10 px-4 py-3 text-emerald-900 dark:text-emerald-200">
        <strong>In summary:</strong> Denaro is a private, offline personal finance
        app. Your financial data stays encrypted on your device. Denaro does not
        collect, transmit, share, or sell your data, and it contains no ads,
        analytics, or tracking services.
    </div>

    <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
    <p>
        Denaro is an Android application for personal finance management developed
        by Mariano Riefolo. It is designed to work entirely offline without an
        account or connection to a remote service.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Data processed on your device</h2>
    <p>
        Denaro processes the information you enter solely on your device to provide
        its finance management features. This may include:
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li>Account names, currencies, and balances</li>
        <li>Income, expenses, transfers, and recurring transactions</li>
        <li>Transaction categories, dates, amounts, and notes</li>
        <li>App preferences such as theme, language, and default currency</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        This on-device processing is necessary for the app to calculate balances,
        display activity, and provide monthly trends and category insights. The
        developer cannot access this information.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Data we do not collect or share</h2>
    <p>Denaro does not collect, transmit, share, or sell:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Financial information entered in the app</li>
        <li>Names, email addresses, or other identifying information</li>
        <li>Location or device identifiers</li>
        <li>Contacts, photos, files, camera, or microphone data</li>
        <li>App usage, analytics, crash reports, or diagnostics</li>
        <li>Advertising identifiers</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        Denaro does not require user registration and does not create or maintain
        user accounts on any server.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Local storage and security</h2>
    <p>Your financial data is protected using the following measures:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <strong>Encrypted database:</strong> financial records are stored in a
            SQLCipher-encrypted database in the app's private storage.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Protected encryption key:</strong> Denaro generates a random
            database passphrase and protects it using a key held by the Android
            Keystore.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>App isolation:</strong> Android isolates the app's private files
            from other apps under normal operating conditions.
        </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        Non-financial preferences, including theme, language, and default currency,
        are stored in the app's private preferences storage.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Network access and permissions</h2>
    <p>
        Denaro does not request Internet access and does not request user-granted
        access to contacts, location, camera, microphone, photos, files, phone
        state, or other sensitive device data.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Advertising, analytics, and third-party services</h2>
    <p>
        Denaro contains no advertising SDKs, analytics services, crash-reporting
        services, social media SDKs, or other tracking technologies. No third party
        receives data from the app.
    </p>
    <p>
        If you obtain Denaro through Google Play, Google may independently process
        information related to store access, downloads, installation, and device
        services. This processing is performed by Google, not by Denaro, and is
        governed by the
        <a
            href="https://policies.google.com/privacy"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="text-[var(--accent-color)] underline underline-offset-2 decoration-2 hover:opacity-80"
        >Google Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Backup and synchronization</h2>
    <p>
        Denaro does not provide cloud synchronization, cloud backup, or data export.
        Its encrypted financial database and associated legacy key material are
        explicitly excluded from Android cloud backups and device-to-device
        transfers.
    </p>
    <p>
        Android may include non-financial app preferences, such as theme, language,
        and default currency, in a system-managed backup according to your device and
        Google account settings. Such backups are controlled by Android and the
        applicable backup provider, not by Denaro.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Data retention and deletion</h2>
    <p>
        Financial data remains on your device until you edit or delete it in Denaro,
        clear the app's storage through Android settings, or uninstall the app.
        Individual financial records can be edited or deleted directly in the app.
    </p>
    <p>
        Clearing app storage or uninstalling Denaro removes its on-device database.
        Because the financial database is excluded from system backup, Denaro does
        not retain a server copy and cannot restore deleted financial data.
        System-managed backups may retain non-financial preferences according to the
        backup provider's retention rules.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Your control over your data</h2>
    <p>Because your financial data stays on your device, you can:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Access:</strong> view your financial records in the app</li>
        <li><strong>Correct:</strong> edit records directly in the app</li>
        <li><strong>Delete:</strong> delete individual records or clear all app data</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        We cannot retrieve, modify, or delete your financial data remotely because
        Denaro never receives it.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Children's privacy</h2>
    <p>
        Denaro does not knowingly collect personal data from children or any other
        users. All information entered in the app remains locally on the user's
        device.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Changes to this Privacy Policy</h2>
    <p>
        This policy may be updated if Denaro's features or data-handling practices
        change. The current version and its latest revision date will always be
        published on this page. Material changes may also be communicated through an
        app update or its Google Play listing.
    </p>

    <div class="my-5 rounded-md border-l-4 border-emerald-500/80 bg-emerald-50/70 dark:bg-emerald-500/10 px-4 py-3 text-emerald-900 dark:text-emerald-200">
        <strong>Remember:</strong> Your financial data stays encrypted on your
        device. Denaro has no server, account system, advertising, analytics, or
        tracking.
    </div>
</PrivacyLayout>
